+Staff can merge duplicate tickets for the same customer with `POST /api/v1/tickets/:id/merge` and a `merge.target_id`. The source is closed, unassigned, and retains its original comments and `merged_into_id` link while the target's status, assignment, and email identity are unchanged. A merge adds a private source note and target note by default; `source_comment` and `target_comment` may each override `body` and `public`. Merge notes never send email. Closed tickets remain readable and appear in `status=closed` staff and customer lists, but cannot be edited or reopened by further replies. Later merges preserve existing merge links.
